~~Button to add another Student // is only enabled when is minor is checked~~
*Design:*
  Guardian ("Who's skating?"): add one or more skaters, each with their full name, "Under 18?" yes or no, skating
    organization and number. "Add another skater" adds more. Each added skater can be removed.
    "Send to Coach <name>" is disabled until at least one skater is added.
  Adult skating themselves ("You're the skater"): their own name from step 2, an "I'm 18 or older" box, and their
    organization and number. A link lets them change who the lessons are for.

Clients must have a USFSA/USA Hockey registration number to sign up. This number is given to them from the USFSA/USA Hockey organization. USA Hockey numbers change each season; US Figure Skating members seem to keep theirs.
    Check to see if there is an API to check if the number is valid for the year/season.  *No way to verify it is valid as of now. Coach can verify themselves if they care*
    *Design:* the number is per skater, not per account. Each skater picks U.S. Figure Skating (member number) or
    USA Hockey (registration number) and enters the number. The hint says USA Hockey numbers change every season.
    *Decided 2026-10-12:* required for every skater. Phase 1 takes USFSA or USA Hockey only; Skate Canada and Hockey Canada are Phase 2.
    *Validation:* the number is a free-text box, so it must be checked and cleaned up before it's saved:
        trim spaces, uppercase, check it against a pattern for its organization (allowed characters only), cap the length,
        and store the cleaned-up form. This checks the shape only, not that the number is real.
        USA Hockey: 14 characters, 9 digits and 5 letters, with a check digit that changes each season (a setting, not code).
        US Figure Skating: format not yet known; get it from a real card or Kim. See ADR-029 and Open-Pending §2b.

Step 5, Waiting for approval:
"You're in", signed in, with each skater listed as waiting for the coach's approval.
The family is emailed when the coach approves. Booking opens for each skater once they're approved.
"Go to my account" button. While waiting, the family sees only Home and Profile (ADR-022 d6, see ClientHomeView).


Profile Icon selection: A list of images uploaded by system phase 2


Clients can have more than one coach. And at signup they put in all of their coaches codes.
